# Why the Apply Decay Threshold is Set to 0.4

1. Defined in code as a design constant with no specific derivation or rationale.
2. The threshold of 0.4 serves as both a decay floor and delete threshold for rule scores.
3. Aging (decay) rules cannot fall below this value, ensuring they remain relevant over time.
